# Kultrun

**Kultrun** is the company and the product. **Company Brain** is the
capability it delivers: a secure, self-hosted organisational intelligence
layer. "AI Deployment Project" and "AI Stack" are retired names.

This repository is a **clean-slate rebuild**. The previous implementation
is evidence, not code structure to preserve. Do not port its modules,
and do not treat its status claims or phase numbers as current.

## Authoritative documents

- @docs/STRATEGY.md — why Kultrun exists, the product/lab split,
 serving-path neutrality, and the four strategic stages. It does not
 own component sequence or module boundaries, and it does not authorize
 Stage 2–4 implementation during the product spine
- @docs/PRODUCT_VISION.md — the product constitution. Authoritative
 for customer experience, domain meaning, and safety semantics
- @docs/machi/ROADMAP.md — authoritative for the active clean-slate
 build sequence. @docs/ROADMAP.md remains the earlier Kultrun
 milestone sequence (0–14) and must not be used to renumber Machi
- @docs/machi/ARCHITECTURE.md — the active module map. Consult it
 before creating any Machi module or import. @docs/ARCHITECTURE.md is
 the Kultrun-lineage map. A change to a module boundary is an edit to
 the active map in the same commit as the code
- @docs/DEBT.md — the debt ledger. Every approximation is recorded here
 with the condition that retires it
- @docs/DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md — branch/GPU workflow **and the
 bounded-step protocol you must follow**
- `docs/legacy/` — previous attempt, retained as evidence only. Never
 authoritative. Read `docs/legacy/README.md` before using anything in it

## Current position

The active build is Machi, not a port of `src/kultrun`. Kernel, Install,
Discover (including mounts and prerequisite readiness), Steward, and
Capacity are accepted on their own checkpoints. Foundation development
is closed: NVIDIA CUDA is physically qualified; AMD ROCm is
implemented and not production-qualified (`M-5-AMD-01`). The next
component is **Model**. Do not start it unless the task says so.

The product spine is still the priority: one real inference path, thin
end to end, before lab comparisons, Dynamo, optimizers, memory, or
Team Brain. The previous attempt wrote 58,706 lines and never reached
that proof. Kultrun on the `kultrun` branch is evidence of a later
native vLLM path, not structure to copy wholesale.

Do not begin later strategic stages early, and do not reintroduce
previous-attempt code to appear further along.

## Governing rules

- Core owns concepts; adapters own implementations.
- Capability-based deployment, not machine-type assumptions.
- Executor and inference runtime are separate abstractions.
- Resource Manager is authoritative for admission. Capacity Planner
  recommends; evidence providers inform and never authorize.
- Only the **safe** capacity layer may authorize an allocation or
  mutation. Reported values may be displayed; they never authorize.
  Raw filesystem capacity never authorizes a storage mutation.
- Unknown is valid and is never zero. Fail conservatively rather than
  invent precision. Feasibility verdicts are never booleans.
- Facts are immutable; policy reinterprets them. An interrupted
  operation is never a success.
- Keep distinct: compatibility / capacity / admission; static / live;
  desired / observed / health; control plane / data plane.
- Identity and permission semantics are shared across Gateway,
  Knowledge, Agents and Admin.
- Prompts, responses, files and RAG content stay local by default.
  Analytics failure never blocks an inference response.
- Every persistent subsystem supports restart and reconciliation.
- Every mutating workflow defines preflight → admission → mutation →
  persistence → rollback/reconciliation.
- Admin UI and Admin Agent consume structured Platform APIs, never
  hidden infrastructure shortcuts.
- Build the exoskeleton thin end-to-end before deepening any part of it.

No third-party technology may become the semantic owner of a platform
concept. Docker, vLLM, Ollama, Dynamo, and LiteLLM are replaceable
adapters or serving paths; native process execution is first class.
Every external evidence provider is advisory with a mandatory internal
fallback.

## Stage discipline

- Produce the stage brief before implementing. For Machi, that brief is the component note under `docs/machi/` and the sequence is `docs/machi/ROADMAP.md`. Kultrun `docs/ROADMAP.md` Part V remains the Kultrun-lineage brief.
- Consume the predecessor's stage output; do not rediscover its facts.
- A stage is done only when it also has failure semantics,
  reconciliation, cleanup/cancellation, a Platform API surface,
  acceptance evidence at the required level, and debt entries. See
  Part II §4.
- `L1` unit evidence never closes a stage that touches hardware, storage
  or a runtime. Milestones 1–4 require `L2` or above.
- End a Kultrun-lineage stage with `docs/stages/STAGE-XX-<name>.md` and
  `checkpoints/STAGE-XX-<name>.json`. End a Machi component with its
  `docs/machi/` package and `checkpoints/MACHI-*.json`.
- If a change is not needed to produce the current stage output, defer
  and record it in `docs/DEBT.md`.
- One concept, one owning module, as assigned in `docs/machi/ARCHITECTURE.md`
  for the active build (`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` Part IV for the Kultrun
  lineage). Never create a near-synonymous module to hold a concept that
  already has an owner.
- Respect the tier dependency law and the declared non-edges in
  `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` Part II. Ports belong to the domain that needs
  them; implementations belong in `adapters/`.
- Renumbering or rescoping a stage requires editing `docs/ROADMAP.md` in
  the same commit as the code.
- Stop refining once the next architectural dependency is unblocked.

## Working rules

- GitHub `dlealvilla/ai-stack` is the source of truth; the slug predates
  the Kultrun name. `kultrun` is the rebuild branch. Do not commit to
  `main`, `phase9` or any `backup/*` branch. Do not push unless
  explicitly asked.
- Never commit secrets, model weights, runtime environments, logs, PID
  files, workload/reservation state or caches. Keep `.gitignore` intact.
- Checkpoints and stage packages record platform state only, never
  customer content.
- Distinguish local/unit evidence from real GPU acceptance when
  reporting runtime behavior.

## Bounded-step protocol

Follow @docs/DEVELOPMENT_WORKFLOW.md:

- Work autonomously inside the active step contract; resolve ordinary
  implementation details from the source, tests and docs rather than asking.
- Stop with `STATE: DECISION_REQUIRED` only at a genuine decision boundary
  (architectural choice, scope expansion, invariant change, unauthorized
  expensive/destructive action, contradicted assumptions, or a product call).
- Record adjacent issues instead of fixing them.
- Finish every development task with the documented `PASTE BACK` block, and
  keep text outside that block minimal.
- Never begin the recommended NEXT step automatically.
